/target
# Cargo.lock is committed: atrium is an application (a binary), so a pinned,
# reproducible dependency graph is checked in for outsider builds. (Library
# crates in the org still gitignore theirs.) Updating an org-crate dep now means
# `cargo update -p <crate>` + committing the refreshed Cargo.lock.

# Workflow worktrees and agent scratch — never part of the tree.
.claude/

# Python bytecode from dev.py — a build artifact, never checked in.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Crash dumps from git-bash / MSYS tools run in this tree.
*.stackdump

# Laid beside the mod by Claude Code whenever it loads or validates mod/: the
# engine's own declarations and a tsconfig extending them, per build.
mod/.claude-plugin/types/
mod/tsconfig.json
